## CODING STANDARDS

## WORKFLOW & RELEASE RULES

*   Building macOS DMG packages for distribution.
*   When building DMGs, if a valid "Developer ID Application" identity or custom non-Apple code signing certificate is not found, the macOS application code signing step will be skipped. Note that this may cause some undefined behavior, such as localized descriptions not being visible. To resolve this, obtain and configure a valid code signing certificate.
*   DMG creation will use APFS if HFS+ is unavailable (macOS 10.12+).
*   Ensure all files required for building the application are included in the &#96;files&#96; array within the &#96;build&#96; section of &#96;package.json&#96;. This includes &#96;main.js&#96;, &#96;preload.js&#96;, and &#96;dist/**/*&#96;.
*   When packaging applications, ensure that the application icon is correctly configured in the &#96;package.json&#96; file. If the icon is missing, electron-builder will use the default Electron icon. Specify the icon path in the &#96;mac&#96; section of the &#96;build&#96; configuration (e.g., &#96;"icon": "icon.icns"&#96;). If an application icon is not explicitly set in the &#96;package.json&#96; file, electron-builder will use the default Electron icon. To avoid this, ensure that the &#96;icon&#96; property within the &#96;mac&#96; section of the &#96;build&#96; configuration is correctly set to the path of your application icon file (e.g., &#96;"icon": "icons/halo.icns"&#96;). If no icon is available, the icon property and related build steps may be skipped to allow the build to proceed.
*   When loading external resources (e.g., Three.js from a CDN), handle potential loading failures gracefully. Provide fallback mechanisms or display informative error messages to the user.
*   When setting the window position, use &#96;mainWindow.setPosition(x, y);&#96; to explicitly set the window's coordinates. Follow this with &#96;mainWindow.show();&#96; and &#96;mainWindow.focus();&#96; to ensure the window is visible and focused.
*   When building for development, load the app from the Vite development server using &#96;mainWindow.loadURL('http://localhost:3000');&#96;.
*   When building for production, load the app from the built files in the &#96;dist&#96; folder using &#96;mainWindow.loadFile('dist/index.html');&#96;.
*   When creating the floating orb widget, ensure the canvas area is non-draggable by setting &#96;-webkit-app-region: no-drag&#96; to allow for user interaction. All elements should have &#96;WebkitAppRegion: 'drag'&#96; for window movement.
*   The main file is specified in &#96;package.json&#96; under the &#96;extraMetadata&#96; property, for example &#96;"extraMetadata": { "main": "main-with-background.js" }&#96;.
*   When building a version of the application with a background, the build command should include a config file, for example: &#96;vite build && electron-builder --mac dmg --config electron-builder-background.config.js&#96;.
*   Copy the DMG file immediately after it's built to avoid it being cleaned by the next build step. For example: &#96;npm run build:dmg && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-Standalone.dmg"&#96;.
*   The build command should be: &#96;npm run build:dmg && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-Standalone.dmg" && npm run build:dmg:background && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget (With Background)-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-With-Background.dmg"&#96;.
*   When creating the standalone widget, the main file in package.json should be &#96;main.js&#96;.
*   When creating the widget with background, the main file in package.json should be &#96;main-with-background.js&#96;.
*   The following commands can be used to build and start the application:
    *   `npm run dev`: Starts the Vite development server.
    *   `npm start`: Starts the Electron application.
    *   `npm run build:dmg`: Builds the standalone application DMG.
    *   `npm run build:dmg:background`: Builds the application DMG with background.
*   When building DMGs, it's necessary to copy the first DMG to a safe location before building the second to prevent electron-builder from cleaning the dist folder.
*   When implementing drag-to-rotate functionality, ensure that the code only responds to right-click (button 2) for rotation, and prevent the context menu from appearing.
*   When creating a build, after building the standalone version, copy it immediately: &#96;npm run build:dmg && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-Standalone.dmg"&#96;.
*   When a project is setup for both a vanilla JavaScript and React version, the build process should account for both.
*   When creating a build that supports both standalone (transparent) and background versions the following build commands should be used:

```
npm run build:dmg && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-Standalone.dmg" && npm run build:dmg:background && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget (With Background)-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-With-Background.dmg"
```

*   Electron-builder cleans the dist folder. Copy the first DMG to a safe location before building the second:

```
npm run build:dmg && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-Standalone.dmg" && npm run build:dmg:background && cp "dist/Floating Orb Widget (With Background)-1.0.0-arm64.dmg" "../Floating-Orb-Widget-With-Background.dmg" && echo "=== BOTH DMG FILES (in parent directory) ===" && ls -lh ../Floating-Orb-Widget*.dmg
```

* When creating a floating widget, ensure that left-click + drag moves the window around screen, and right-click + drag rotates the sphere. Follow these steps:
    * Set -webkit-app-region: drag on the body/container to enable window dragging.
    * Set -webkit-app-region: no-drag on the canvas but handle right-click for rotation.
    * Update the pointer handlers to only respond to right-click (button 2) for rotation.
* The following CSS should be applied to the body to ensure proper functioning of the frameless widget with drag and rotate:

```css
body {
  width: 100vw;
  height: 100vh;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: transparent;
  -webkit-app-region: drag; /* Make window draggable */
}
```
* When implementing combined window movement and sphere rotation with the mouse remember to:
    *   Stop event propagation: Use e.stopPropagation() in event handlers to prevent conflicts between canvas interaction and window dragging.
    *   Disable context menu: Prevent the context menu from appearing on right-click to enable smooth rotation.
